\citation{gat2025anytop}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Extending \textsc  {TopX}{} (\textcolor {blue}{303}M) to four Truebones rigs, as a diagnostic given the rig's statistics: the per-cell statistics and masks of each rig are computed from all of its clips, the evaluation clips included, and the adapter checkpoint is the one with the lowest validation loss on those clips (a support-only protocol is reported in the final version). \emph  {zero}: library model with the rig's statistics only (gap read after at most 15 adapter warm-up steps); \emph  {LoRA}: per-rig adapter at its best validation loss; \emph  {TB-only}: a \textcolor {blue}{36}M model trained on all Truebones clips including these (seen-clip reference; its gap is read the same way as the zero column). Gap in bone lengths; articulation and jitter of the sampled FK output relative to all real clips of the rig (1 = real). The same study on the \textcolor {blue}{36}M pilot backbone, and a single adapter shared by eight flying rigs, are in App.~\ref {app:extend_more}.}}{9}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:lora}{{2}{9}{Extending \method {} (\num {303}M) to four Truebones rigs, as a diagnostic given the rig's statistics: the per-cell statistics and masks of each rig are computed from all of its clips, the evaluation clips included, and the adapter checkpoint is the one with the lowest validation loss on those clips (a support-only protocol is reported in the final version). \emph {zero}: library model with the rig's statistics only (gap read after at most 15 adapter warm-up steps); \emph {LoRA}: per-rig adapter at its best validation loss; \emph {TB-only}: a \num {36}M model trained on all Truebones clips including these (seen-clip reference; its gap is read the same way as the zero column). Gap in bone lengths; articulation and jitter of the sampled FK output relative to all real clips of the rig (1 = real). The same study on the \num {36}M pilot backbone, and a single adapter shared by eight flying rigs, are in App.~\ref {app:extend_more}}{table.2}{}}
